    "visionGoal":  "Navigate Alan Wake II\u0027s cold-launch screens to its MAIN MENU and then STOP. The MAIN MENU is a VERTICAL LIST of several short options STACKED on the LEFT side of the screen (the options are CONTINUE, NEW GAME, SETTINGS, EXTRAS and QUIT, drawn as low-contrast light-gray text over a dark, moody background β€” you may only be able to clearly read ONE or TWO of them, and that is fine; recognize it by the LAYOUT: a column of several stacked text options on the left). Choose ONE action: answer DONE the moment you see that vertical stack of TWO OR MORE menu options on the left β€” and do NOT press anything, the rest of the run is fully automated from the menu. Answer CONFIRM ONLY to advance a SINGLE press-to-start prompt that is NOT a list β€” e.g. a title/attract screen showing \u0027PRESS ANY BUTTON\u0027 or \u0027ENTER CONTINUE\u0027 centered on screen. Answer WAIT for: a studio/publisher logo; a loading spinner or progress bar; a \u0027GAME SAVING - do not turn off\u0027 screen; OR a cinematic story/chapter card that shows a PARAGRAPH of narrative prose with a small \u0027Next\u0027 prompt (a paragraph of story text means a game has ALREADY STARTED β€” NEVER CONFIRM it, only WAIT). CRITICAL RULES: (1) NEVER answer CONFIRM while a vertical LIST of menu options is visible β€” that would start the game; answer DONE instead. (2) A single highlighted CONTINUE button by itself, or any screen with a paragraph of prose text, is NOT the main menu β€” only a column of several stacked options is. (3) If you are unsure between CONFIRM and DONE and you can see more than one stacked option on the left, ALWAYS choose DONE.",
